A||N||8||fropuff||Hard starting--6 cyl||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||08-09-2001||12:23 AM||||Hey guys.  It's pretty hot out, and I've noticed that my 86 GT doesn't start like it did before.  Before, it started fine, but now, I have to crank it a little more.  Now I need to crank it for 3-5 seconds for it to start.  It runs fine after that, but it's a little annoying.  Any ideas?  Thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Fiero:  If it ain't broke, it's on fire.  If it ain't on fire, it's broke.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||08-09-2001||05:20 AM||||fuel pump relay is probably going, or gone already, so the oil pump relay has taken over.  The oil pump relay needs 4 psi of oil pressure to "start" everything, so you have to crank it for a few seconds, especially in this weather.<P>If this sounds confusing... that's cause i should be in bed..<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||08-09-2001||09:26 AM||||Makes sense; I get it.  So all I need is a relay, not the fuel pump assembly?  Am I hurting anything if I wait until Saturday or Sunday to fix it?  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||08-09-2001||09:30 AM||||My car did this for a while. A quick fix was pulling the relay and cleaning it.<P>I went to buy a new one , but the local parts store (Crappy tire) Did not have a listing for a fuel pump relay on the car.<P>Guy said it must not have one..and thats why he is paid the big bucks.<P>Anyone have an idea where to get one and how much?? I can get stuff from a GM dealership at 10% over cost..<P>Now the relay stays on and the fuel pump is constantly going...Pulled the fuse<P>Thanks!<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||08-09-2001||09:38 AM||||Since I'm Fiero inept, I was wondering if someone could tell me where the fuel pump relay is located.  What do you use to clean it?  I'll try to find another; just a temporary fix.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||08-09-2001||12:51 PM||||It's one of the two little boxes with wires coming out of it on the drivers side of the front firewall, i think.||||reg||1
Z||000006||starfighter007@msn.com||08-09-2001||01:10 PM||||Standered, is right that is where the relay is but Dont remember which one is which. I think it is the one closest to the outside of the car but what if someone moved them around?yikes.. I am confused,I know somebody here knows how to tell them apart. I wonder how do you tell them apart colors of the wires?and I think these two relays are the same One is for a/c other one is for the fuel pump.If so can't you just swap the relay plugs for diagnostic purposes?Hmmm I wonder  Ogre will set us straight on this one||||reg||10
Z||000007||2birds||08-09-2001||08:11 PM||||Before you spend the money on a rely, do this first.  When you go to start the car, put the key in run, and you should here the fuel pump come on for about 2 seconds, then shut off.  It won't do this immediately after shutdown or right after you already did it, so listen carefully the first time you try it it.  The ECM energizes the rely to turn on the fuel pump to build up pressure until the engine is running, then when the oil pressure is high enough, the oil pressure switch bypasses the fuel pump relay completely.  <BR>My hard starting problem was a combination of the fuel pump relay and a bad (falling apart after 160,000 miles) distributor pick up coil.||||reg||1
Z||000008||dgroves||08-11-2001||01:07 PM||||The two relays on the firewall behind the drivers seat are the fuel pump and A/C compressor relays. Yes they are the same part. as a matter of fact there are several more of them. (Air blower, headlamp motors .......) Relay is common to most GM cars. Can't imagine an auto parts store that dosen't carry this item! My car does the same thing. I replaced the relay and didn't solve the problem. Then I replaced the ECM and didn't solve the problem. Still can't figure out what's going on.||||reg||1
